OL,3,GNEWSA'If you want something beautiful
OL,4,Ain your town, you've got to love it'
OL,5,
OL,6,F"I've got a lot of fond memories of
OL,7,Fwalking through the market and the
OL,8,Farcade with my grandma as a little
OL,9,Fgirl. So it feels like a real 360 to be
OL,10,Fback here."
OL,12,FStanding in the doorway of her brand
OL,13,Fnew unit in Dewsbury Arcade, Emily
OL,14,FParkinson is delighted with the
OL,15,Frecently-installed bell, which will
OL,16,Falert her when customers cross the
OL,17,Fthreshold.
OL,19,FEmily and the 15 other vendors are
OL,20,Fhoping to hear that sound on repeat,
OL,21,Fwhen the building opens on 5 September.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
